{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And they shall lean.</b> Why was this one singled out for leaning hands from among all those liable to death penalties? Because at the time of completing the verdict, the judges needed to say to the witnesses: state explicitly what you heard. And the witnesses would state explicitly ברכת השם, exactly as they heard it. Therefore they would lean their hands on him, meaning: this sin that we are committing, to bless HaShem's name, shall hang on your neck, for you caused it. All who hear the testimony are stoned." "<b>And they shall stone him.</b> Because he converted, for had he not converted he would not have been stoned, for a Son of Noah's judgment is by the sword, with witnesses and warning. We heard the punishment; the warning — from where? For a Son of Noah, from ״ויצו יהוה Elohim על האדם״; for an Israelite, from ״אלהים לא תקלל״. <b>him</b> — and not his garment."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:57.424240660Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}